After adjustment for baseline ESS, the observed treatment effect is -2.7 (95% CI -5.1 to -0.35, p = 0.027), showing a modest and statistically significant effect of didgeridoo playing on sleep apnea. These are essentially the results that @didgeridoo reported, though they examined change scores.


